Every website is HTML: elements written as tags in angle brackets that can be nested inside each other. A page has four main tags: &lt;html&gt; wraps everything, &lt;head&gt; loads stylesheets and metadata, &lt;title&gt; names the page, and &lt;body&gt; holds everything visitors see.

